within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01C_BetaLactamAntibacterialsPenicillins.J01CA04_Amoxicillin;
model Amoxicillin "Amoxicillin — default model: Amoxicillin_Lacampagne2026_reference"
  extends Amoxicillin_Lacampagne2026_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of amoxicillin: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01C_BetaLactamAntibacterialsPenicillins.J01CA04_Amoxicillin.Amoxicillin_Lacampagne2026_reference\">Amoxicillin_Lacampagne2026_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of amoxicillin in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_cat_1</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_cat_2</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_cat_3</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_cat_4</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_cat_5</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_median</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Dubbelboer2025_typical_value</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Lacampagne2026_reference</code></li><li><code>Amoxicillin_Wu2021_reference</code></li></ul><h4>About amoxicillin</h4><p>Amoxicillin is a penicillin antibiotic used to treat many bacterial infections, including ear, sinus, respiratory and urinary tract infections, and it is also given in combination to eradicate Helicobacter pylori. It is widely used around the world, is included on the WHO list of essential medicines, and is also approved for veterinary use.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q201928\">Wikidata Q201928</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Amoxicillin\">Amoxicillin</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>10/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Amoxicillin;
